 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-zqLU_ipcZv0/WT9vaN9S1yI/AAAAAAAAdp4/j4e-5OLPDCgcqWAdJ_vHlr-Q8Lkp4cjxQCLcB/s1600/Rplot57.png>
Listing all the states in each facet wastes space, since each state appears in only one facet. You can use `scales="free_x"` and `space="free_x"` in order to have each state appear only in its region. Here's an example with built-in data:

set.seed(2)
dat = data.frame(state=rep(state.abb,100), region=rep(state.region,100), value=rnorm(50*100))

ggplot(dat, aes(state, value)) +
  geom_boxplot(width=0.5, outlier.color=NA, fill="red") +
  facet_grid(. ~ region, scales="free_x", space="free_x") +
  theme_classic()

