To set the axis ranges separately for each facet I think you actually need to create a separate plot for what was formerly each facet (which gives you direct control over the x-range for each facet) and then lay the plots out together as if they had been generated using facet_wrap. Here <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36432292/ggplot2-how-can-i-set-axis-breaks-separately-for-each-facet-in-facet-wrap/36432976#36432976> and here <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/30280499/different-y-limits-on-ggplot-facet-grid-bar-graph/30281595#30281595> are a couple of examples from answers I've written on Stack Overflow and I'm sure there are other examples on SO as well.

