MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Good morning,

When specifying the number of rows in facet_wrap, is there a way to set it conditionally, based on the number of plots? I'm making multi-page PDFs with one page per group of multiple graphs, and each group has a different number of associated graphs on the page. I'd want to specify, if there are x number of graphs, use y rows, a number of graphs, use z rows, etc.

Thanks!

Stefanie Trop

From ubfc2eb6b71169017 at groups.google.com  Fri Jun 30 16:10:54 2017
From: ubfc2eb6b71169017 at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?q?Roman_Lu=C5=A1trik?=)
Date: Fri, 30 Jun 2017 16:10:54 +0000
Subject: Re: Conditional nrows in facetting
Message-ID: <hLuE0D-gEZc.FJK-XxheBgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <hLuE0D-gEZc.At0zkU1dBgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <hLuE0D-gEZc.At0zkU1dBgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/hLuE0D-gEZc/m/FJK-XxheBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Number of graphs in your case is probably the number of levels. If that's true, you could adapt the number of rows dynamically.

Something along the lines of

> nr <- ifelse(length(levels(x))  == 6, 3, else 2) # something smart here
> ggplot(...) + facet_warp(..., nrow = nr)

Cheers,
Roman

